<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5628" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bracchĭŏlum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">brāch-</span></b> ), i,
			n.
		dim.
		bracchium. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A small</i>, <i>delicate arm</i>:
			puellulae, * <i><span class="en">Cat. 61,
			181</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A muscle in a horse</i>'<i>s leg</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Veg. 1, 25, 4</span></i> and 5; cf.
					<i><span class="en">id. 6, 1, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 2,
			2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">5, 27, 7</span></i>; 5, 70, 2.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The arm</i> of a chair or seat, <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2 Par.
				9, 18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
